    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005",
      "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
      "finding": "Within-game and cross-game inferred defensive scheme change rates are very high (61-68%), but the near-uniform transition matrices are consistent with label noise. The inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from the offense executing differently."
